config {
  type:"table",
  schema:"reportdb",
  name:"dash_trend_monthly",
  description:"Monthly channel trend at level_2 grain. Adds metric parity with dash_trend_weekly (gmv, units, aov, asp, customers, discount), MoM deltas, trailing 6-month shape, the full run-rate block (pro-rated target, projection, required daily NMV) and data-quality trust flags. All pre-existing columns are unchanged in name, type, order and value."
}

/* =============================================================================
   dash_trend_monthly
   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   WHAT CHANGED, AND WHY

   1. RUN-RATE. The table could say where the month stands but not where it is
      heading. attainment_vs_full_month answers "how much of plan is banked";
      it cannot answer "will we land". nmv_run_rate_full_month, projected_
      attainment and required_daily_nmv close that, and required_vs_recent_ratio
      states the ask in the only unit an ops team can act on: how much harder
      each remaining day has to work than the days already traded.

   2. THE PRO-RATED TARGET MOVES INTO SQL. v_dash_ai_facts_core computes
      attainment against the pro-rated MTD target inline, and comments there warn
      that pairing it with "day N of M" states the opposite of the truth. Both
      denominators now live here as named columns, so the prompt reads them
      rather than deriving them.

   3. TARGET FAN-OUT HARDENED. The tgt CTE used SELECT DISTINCT together with
      GROUP BY 1,2,3,4 where position 4 was month_target_revenue itself. It does
      not duplicate today (60 rows, 60 keys), but grouping by the measure means
      the day a single (month, country, level_2) ever carries two target values
      the FULL OUTER JOIN silently doubles the actuals. MAX() removes that.

   4. CUTOFF IS NOW COUNTRY-AWARE. cut grouped by level_2 alone, so a channel
      name reused across countries - 'VN Online' exists under both VIETNAM and
      THAILAND - let one country's late feed truncate another's. No-op on
      current data; it stops being a no-op the first time a feed slips.

   5. THE CUTOFF IS NOW VISIBLE. It is deliberately conservative: MIN() across a
      channel, so TQ Ecommerce is read only through Tmall/Taobao's Sunday upload
      even though Douyin and Xiaohongshu are current. In the first days of a
      month that can show a channel at zero MTD against a full-month target, and
      nothing in the old output said so. days_covered, is_month_data_complete and
      nmv_excluded_by_cutoff now say it explicitly.

   GRAIN: month_start x country x level_1 x level_2   (unchanged)
   ========================================================================== */

WITH p AS (SELECT * FROM ${ref("dash_run_params")}),

cut AS (
  SELECT
     country
    ,level_2
    ,MIN(data_complete_through) AS cutoff
    ,MAX(last_date_with_data)   AS last_data
  FROM ${ref("dash_dq_platform_day")}
  GROUP BY country, level_2
),

base AS (
  SELECT
     DATE_TRUNC(b.period_date, MONTH) AS month_start
    ,b.country, b.level_1, b.level_2
    ,b.period_date, b.order_id, b.customer_id
    ,IF(IS_NAN(b.nmv)        OR b.nmv        IS NULL, 0, b.nmv)        AS nmv
    ,IF(IS_NAN(b.gmv)        OR b.gmv        IS NULL, 0, b.gmv)        AS gmv
    ,IF(IS_NAN(b.units_sold) OR b.units_sold IS NULL, 0, b.units_sold) AS units
    ,IFNULL(b.has_true_gmv, FALSE)                    AS has_true_gmv
    ,IFNULL(b.nmv_basis, '')                          AS nmv_basis
    ,b.period_date <= IFNULL(c.cutoff, b.period_date) AS in_scope
    ,c.cutoff                                         AS data_complete_through
    ,c.last_data                                      AS last_date_with_data
  FROM ${ref("dash_base_order_day")} b
  LEFT JOIN cut c
    ON c.country = b.country AND c.level_2 = b.level_2
  CROSS JOIN p
  WHERE b.period_date >= DATE_SUB(DATE_TRUNC(p.report_date, MONTH), INTERVAL 5 MONTH)
    AND b.period_date <= p.report_date
),

/* ============================ DAYS-ELAPSED CAPPING ==========================
   N = mtd_days_elapsed, the days elapsed in the current calendar month.

   The month-on-month columns previously took the prior month IN FULL from the
   `wprev` window, while `nmv` for the current row holds only N days. Measured on
   2026-09-04 at day 3 of 30, that made every channel read as a collapse:

     VIETNAM / VN Ecommerce      403m vs 4,746m   = -92%
     VIETNAM / VN Offline Store  346m vs 6,607m   = -95%
     CHINA   / TQ Ecommerce        0m vs 7,611m   = -100%

   None of that is trade. It is 3 days measured against 30.

   The current month is therefore compared against days 1..N of the PRIOR month.
   A CLOSED month keeps full-vs-full, which is already like-for-like and is what
   completed reporting depends on.
   ========================================================================== */
mom_window AS (
  SELECT
     p.mtd_days_elapsed                                            AS n_days
    ,DATE_TRUNC(p.report_date, MONTH)                              AS cur_start
    ,p.report_date                                                 AS cur_end
    ,DATE_SUB(DATE_TRUNC(p.report_date, MONTH), INTERVAL 1 MONTH)  AS prv_start
    -- clamped to the prior month's own last day: at N=31 against a 30-day prior
    -- month the window would otherwise spill a day into the month before this one
    ,LEAST(
       DATE_ADD(DATE_SUB(DATE_TRUNC(p.report_date, MONTH), INTERVAL 1 MONTH),
                INTERVAL p.mtd_days_elapsed - 1 DAY),
       LAST_DAY(DATE_SUB(DATE_TRUNC(p.report_date, MONTH), INTERVAL 1 MONTH))
     )                                                             AS prv_end
  FROM p
),

-- Prior month capped to days 1..N. Same in_scope cutoff as `act`, so the two
-- sides of the comparison are filtered identically.
prev_capped AS (
  SELECT
     b.country, b.level_2
    ,SUM(b.nmv)                                      AS nmv
    ,SUM(b.units)                                    AS units
    ,COUNT(DISTINCT IF(b.nmv > 0, b.order_id, NULL)) AS bills
    ,SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(b.nmv),
       NULLIF(COUNT(DISTINCT IF(b.nmv > 0, b.order_id, NULL)),0))  AS aov
  FROM base b CROSS JOIN mom_window mw
  WHERE b.in_scope
    AND b.period_date BETWEEN mw.prv_start AND mw.prv_end
  GROUP BY 1,2
),

-- The trailing-6-month baseline has the same defect: a 3-day month compared to
-- an average of full months is an outlier by construction. For the current row
-- the baseline is rebuilt from the first N days of each prior month.
prev6_capped AS (
  SELECT
     country, level_2
    ,AVG(m_nmv)         AS nmv_avg_6m_same_elapsed
    ,STDDEV_SAMP(m_nmv) AS nmv_stddev_6m_same_elapsed
    ,MIN(m_nmv)         AS nmv_min_6m_same_elapsed
    ,MAX(m_nmv)         AS nmv_max_6m_same_elapsed
  FROM (
    SELECT b.country, b.level_2, DATE_TRUNC(b.period_date, MONTH) AS m,
           SUM(b.nmv) AS m_nmv
    FROM base b CROSS JOIN mom_window mw
    WHERE b.in_scope
      AND DATE_TRUNC(b.period_date, MONTH) < mw.cur_start
      AND EXTRACT(DAY FROM b.period_date) <= mw.n_days   -- first N days of each month
    GROUP BY 1,2,3
  )
  GROUP BY 1,2
),

-- WHERE in_scope, not a conditional SUM. A month whose every row sits beyond the
-- cutoff must produce NO act row, exactly as the original WHERE clause did, so
-- that the row still arrives from the target side of the FULL OUTER JOIN with a
-- NULL level_1 and a NULL attainment. Aggregating with IF(in_scope,...) instead
-- would manufacture a zero row and silently turn seven NULL attainments into
-- 0%, which dash_material_points would then flag as -100pp off pace.
act AS (
  SELECT
     month_start, country, level_1, level_2
    ,SUM(nmv)                                        AS nmv
    ,SUM(gmv)                                        AS gmv
    ,SUM(units)                                      AS units
    ,COUNT(DISTINCT IF(nmv > 0, order_id, NULL))     AS bills
    ,COUNT(DISTINCT order_id)                        AS bills_incl_zero
    ,COUNT(DISTINCT NULLIF(customer_id,''))          AS customers
    ,COUNT(DISTINCT period_date)                     AS days_covered
    ,SUM(IF(has_true_gmv, gmv, 0))                   AS gmv_observed
    ,SUM(IF(has_true_gmv, nmv, 0))                   AS nmv_on_observed_gmv
    ,SUM(IF(STARTS_WITH(nmv_basis,'modelled'), nmv, 0)) AS nmv_modelled
  FROM base
  WHERE in_scope
  GROUP BY 1,2,3,4
),

-- What the cutoff withheld, measured separately so it can be reported without
-- creating a row that would not otherwise exist.
excl AS (
  SELECT month_start, country, level_2, SUM(nmv) AS nmv_excluded_by_cutoff
  FROM base
  WHERE NOT in_scope
  GROUP BY 1,2,3
),

-- MAX() instead of grouping by the measure: month_target_revenue is constant
-- within (month_start, country, level_2), and the moment it is not, grouping by
-- it would fan the FULL OUTER JOIN out and double the actuals.
tgt AS (
  SELECT
     t.month_start
    ,t.country
    ,t.level_2
    ,MAX(t.level_1)                        AS level_1_target
    ,MAX(t.month_target_revenue)           AS month_target
    ,LOGICAL_OR(t.is_low_target)           AS is_low_target
    ,LOGICAL_OR(t.is_target_invalid)       AS is_target_invalid
    ,LOGICAL_OR(t.is_unmapped_channel)     AS is_unmapped_channel
    ,LOGICAL_OR(t.is_multi_country_target) AS is_multi_country_target
  FROM ${ref("dash_target_day")} t
  CROSS JOIN p
  WHERE t.sale_date >= DATE_SUB(DATE_TRUNC(p.report_date, MONTH), INTERVAL 5 MONTH)
    AND t.sale_date <= LAST_DAY(p.report_date)
  GROUP BY 1,2,3
),

j AS (
  SELECT
     COALESCE(a.month_start, t.month_start)   AS month_start
    ,COALESCE(a.country, t.country)           AS country
    ,a.level_1
    ,COALESCE(a.level_1, t.level_1_target)    AS level_1_resolved
    ,COALESCE(a.level_2, t.level_2)           AS level_2
    -- nullable on purpose: a target-only month has no actual, and NULL is what
    -- the attainment and pace columns have always been fed there
    ,a.nmv                                    AS nmv_raw
    ,IFNULL(a.nmv,   0)                       AS nmv
    ,IFNULL(a.gmv,   0)                       AS gmv
    ,IFNULL(a.units, 0)                       AS units
    ,IFNULL(a.bills, 0)                       AS bills
    ,IFNULL(a.bills_incl_zero, 0)             AS bills_incl_zero
    ,IFNULL(a.customers, 0)                   AS customers
    ,IFNULL(a.days_covered, 0)                AS days_covered
    ,a.month_start IS NOT NULL                AS has_actuals
    ,IFNULL(e.nmv_excluded_by_cutoff, 0)      AS nmv_excluded_by_cutoff
    ,IFNULL(a.gmv_observed, 0)                AS gmv_observed
    ,IFNULL(a.nmv_on_observed_gmv, 0)         AS nmv_on_observed_gmv
    ,IFNULL(a.nmv_modelled, 0)                AS nmv_modelled
    ,c.cutoff                                 AS data_complete_through
    ,c.last_data                              AS last_date_with_data
    ,t.month_target
    ,IFNULL(t.is_low_target,           FALSE) AS is_low_target
    ,IFNULL(t.is_target_invalid,       FALSE) AS is_target_invalid
    ,IFNULL(t.is_unmapped_channel,     FALSE) AS is_unmapped_channel
    ,IFNULL(t.is_multi_country_target, FALSE) AS is_multi_country_target
  FROM act a
  FULL OUTER JOIN tgt t
    ON  a.month_start = t.month_start
    AND a.country     = t.country
    AND a.level_2     = t.level_2
  LEFT JOIN excl e
    ON  e.month_start = COALESCE(a.month_start, t.month_start)
    AND e.country     = COALESCE(a.country,     t.country)
    AND e.level_2     = COALESCE(a.level_2,     t.level_2)
  LEFT JOIN cut c
    ON  c.country     = COALESCE(a.country, t.country)
    AND c.level_2     = COALESCE(a.level_2, t.level_2)
),

-- Dense month index so the trailing windows survive a month with no rows.
-- Ordering on the raw date with RANGE would measure in days, not months.
ix AS (
  SELECT
     j.*
    ,EXTRACT(YEAR FROM DATE(j.month_start)) * 12
       + EXTRACT(MONTH FROM DATE(j.month_start))            AS month_idx
    ,DATE(j.month_start) = DATE_TRUNC(p.report_date, MONTH) AS is_current_month
    ,IF(DATE(j.month_start) = DATE_TRUNC(p.report_date, MONTH),
        p.mtd_days_elapsed,
        DATE_DIFF(LAST_DAY(DATE(j.month_start)), DATE(j.month_start), DAY) + 1) AS days_elapsed
    ,DATE_DIFF(LAST_DAY(DATE(j.month_start)), DATE(j.month_start), DAY) + 1     AS days_total
    ,SAFE_DIVIDE(j.nmv,   NULLIF(j.bills,0))      AS aov
    ,SAFE_DIVIDE(j.units, NULLIF(j.bills,0))      AS units_per_bill
    ,SAFE_DIVIDE(j.nmv,   NULLIF(j.units,0))      AS asp
    ,SAFE_DIVIDE(j.bills, NULLIF(j.customers,0))  AS bills_per_customer
    ,IF(j.gmv_observed > 0,
        1 - SAFE_DIVIDE(j.nmv_on_observed_gmv, j.gmv_observed), NULL) AS discount_rate
    ,SAFE_DIVIDE(j.nmv_on_observed_gmv, NULLIF(j.nmv,0)) AS pct_gmv_observed
    ,SAFE_DIVIDE(j.nmv_modelled,        NULLIF(j.nmv,0)) AS pct_nmv_modelled
  FROM j CROSS JOIN p
),

w AS (
  SELECT
     ix.*
    ,MAX(ix.nmv)        OVER wprev AS nmv_prev_month_full
    ,MAX(ix.bills)      OVER wprev AS bills_prev_month_full
    ,MAX(ix.aov)        OVER wprev AS aov_prev_month_full
    ,MAX(ix.units)      OVER wprev AS units_prev_month_full
    ,MIN(ix.nmv)        OVER w6    AS nmv_min_6m
    ,MAX(ix.nmv)        OVER w6    AS nmv_max_6m
    ,AVG(ix.nmv)        OVER w6    AS nmv_avg_6m
    ,STDDEV_SAMP(ix.nmv) OVER w6   AS nmv_stddev_6m
    ,COUNT(*)           OVER w6    AS months_available
    ,AVG(ix.nmv)        OVER w3    AS nmv_ma3
    ,SUM(ix.nmv) OVER (PARTITION BY ix.month_start, ix.country) AS nmv_country
    ,SUM(ix.nmv) OVER (PARTITION BY ix.month_start)             AS nmv_group
  FROM ix
  WINDOW
     wprev AS (PARTITION BY ix.country, ix.level_2 ORDER BY ix.month_idx
               RANGE BETWEEN 1 PRECEDING AND 1 PRECEDING)
    ,w6    AS (PARTITION BY ix.country, ix.level_2 ORDER BY ix.month_idx
               RANGE BETWEEN 6 PRECEDING AND 1 PRECEDING)
    ,w3    AS (PARTITION BY ix.country, ix.level_2 ORDER BY ix.month_idx
               RANGE BETWEEN 3 PRECEDING AND 1 PRECEDING)
),

calc AS (
  SELECT
     w.*
    ,SAFE_DIVIDE(w.days_elapsed, NULLIF(w.days_total,0))            AS elapsed_share
    -- attainment is always against the FULL-MONTH target, so the series is comparable
    ,IF(w.is_low_target OR w.is_target_invalid, NULL,
        SAFE_DIVIDE(w.nmv_raw, NULLIF(w.month_target,0)))           AS attainment_vs_full_month
    ,IF(w.is_current_month,
        SAFE_DIVIDE(p.mtd_days_elapsed, p.month_total_days), 1.0)   AS expected_pace
    -- daily rate measured on days actually READ, not days elapsed: a channel
    -- held back by the completeness cutoff must not be projected as if it traded
    -- and sold nothing
    ,SAFE_DIVIDE(w.nmv, NULLIF(w.days_covered,0))                   AS recent_daily_nmv
  FROM w CROSS JOIN p
),

proj AS (
  SELECT
     calc.*
    ,calc.month_target * calc.elapsed_share                         AS mtd_target_prorated
    ,IF(calc.is_low_target OR calc.is_target_invalid, NULL,
        SAFE_DIVIDE(calc.nmv_raw, NULLIF(calc.month_target * calc.elapsed_share,0)))
                                                                    AS attainment_vs_prorated
    ,IF(calc.is_current_month,
        calc.recent_daily_nmv * calc.days_total, calc.nmv)          AS nmv_run_rate_full_month
    ,IF(calc.is_current_month AND calc.days_total > calc.days_elapsed,
        SAFE_DIVIDE(calc.month_target - calc.nmv,
                    NULLIF(calc.days_total - calc.days_elapsed,0)), NULL)
                                                                    AS required_daily_nmv
  FROM calc
),

-- Run of consecutive months that missed plan, ending at this month. The run
-- breaks on a gap as well as on a hit, so a channel that stopped trading does
-- not have two distant misses read as consecutive.
streak AS (
  SELECT
     s.*
    ,SUM(new_run) OVER (PARTITION BY country, level_2 ORDER BY month_idx
                        ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW) AS run_id
  FROM (
    SELECT
       proj.*
      ,IF(    IFNULL(attainment_vs_full_month, 1) < 1
          AND IFNULL(LAG(attainment_vs_full_month)
                       OVER (PARTITION BY country, level_2 ORDER BY month_idx), 1) < 1
          AND LAG(month_idx) OVER (PARTITION BY country, level_2 ORDER BY month_idx)
              = month_idx - 1,
          0, 1) AS new_run
    FROM proj
  ) s
)

SELECT
   -- ---------- EXISTING CONTRACT: names, types, order and values unchanged ----
   s.month_start
  ,s.country
  ,s.level_1
  ,s.level_2
  ,s.nmv
  ,s.bills
  ,s.month_target
  ,s.is_current_month
  ,s.attainment_vs_full_month
  ,s.expected_pace
  ,IF(s.is_low_target OR s.is_target_invalid, NULL,
      (s.attainment_vs_full_month - s.expected_pace) * 100) AS pace_gap_pp
  ,s.is_low_target
  ,s.is_target_invalid
  ,s.is_unmapped_channel

   -- ---------- NEW: metric parity with dash_trend_weekly ---------------------
  ,s.gmv
  ,s.units
  ,s.bills_incl_zero
  ,s.aov
  ,s.units_per_bill
  ,s.asp
  ,s.customers
  ,s.bills_per_customer
  ,s.discount_rate
  ,s.pct_gmv_observed
  ,s.level_1_resolved                                       -- level_1 filled in on target-only rows
  ,s.has_actuals                                            -- FALSE = plan exists, nothing traded/readable
  ,s.is_multi_country_target

   -- ---------- month-on-month, CAPPED TO THE SAME DAYS ELAPSED ---------------
   -- >>> DAYS-ELAPSED CAPPING APPLIED HERE <<<
   -- Current row: days 1..N of this month  vs  days 1..N of the prior month.
   -- Closed row : full month vs full prior month, unchanged.
  ,IF(s.is_current_month, pc.nmv,   s.nmv_prev_month_full)   AS nmv_prev_month
  ,IF(s.is_current_month, pc.bills, s.bills_prev_month_full) AS bills_prev_month
  ,IF(s.is_current_month, pc.aov,   s.aov_prev_month_full)   AS aov_prev_month
  ,IF(s.is_current_month, pc.units, s.units_prev_month_full) AS units_prev_month
   -- uncapped prior month kept alongside, so nothing that needed it is lost
  ,s.nmv_prev_month_full
  ,s.bills_prev_month_full
  ,s.aov_prev_month_full
  ,s.units_prev_month_full
  ,s.nmv - IF(s.is_current_month, pc.nmv, s.nmv_prev_month_full)  AS nmv_mom_abs
  ,SAFE_DIVIDE(s.nmv,
     NULLIF(IF(s.is_current_month, pc.nmv,   s.nmv_prev_month_full),0))   - 1 AS nmv_mom_pct
  ,SAFE_DIVIDE(s.bills,
     NULLIF(IF(s.is_current_month, pc.bills, s.bills_prev_month_full),0)) - 1 AS bills_mom_pct
  ,SAFE_DIVIDE(s.aov,
     NULLIF(IF(s.is_current_month, pc.aov,   s.aov_prev_month_full),0))   - 1 AS aov_mom_pct
   -- the two windows stated explicitly, so the comparison is auditable
  ,s.is_current_month                                       AS mom_window_capped
  ,IF(s.is_current_month, mw.n_days,
      EXTRACT(DAY FROM LAST_DAY(DATE_SUB(DATE(s.month_start), INTERVAL 1 MONTH))))
                                                            AS mom_compare_days
  ,IF(s.is_current_month, mw.cur_start, DATE(s.month_start)) AS mom_cur_period_start
  ,IF(s.is_current_month, mw.cur_end, LAST_DAY(DATE(s.month_start)))
                                                            AS mom_cur_period_end
  ,IF(s.is_current_month, mw.prv_start,
      DATE_SUB(DATE(s.month_start), INTERVAL 1 MONTH))       AS mom_prv_period_start
  ,IF(s.is_current_month, mw.prv_end,
      LAST_DAY(DATE_SUB(DATE(s.month_start), INTERVAL 1 MONTH)))
                                                            AS mom_prv_period_end

   -- ---------- NEW: trailing 6-month shape -----------------------------------
  ,s.nmv_ma3
  ,s.nmv_min_6m
  ,s.nmv_max_6m
  ,s.nmv_avg_6m
  ,s.nmv_stddev_6m
  ,s.months_available
   -- >>> DAYS-ELAPSED CAPPING APPLIED HERE <<<  the current partial month is
   -- indexed against the prior months' FIRST N DAYS, not their full totals.
  ,SAFE_DIVIDE(s.nmv,
     NULLIF(IF(s.is_current_month, p6.nmv_avg_6m_same_elapsed, s.nmv_avg_6m),0))
                                                            AS nmv_index_vs_6m_avg
  ,SAFE_DIVIDE(
     s.nmv - IF(s.is_current_month, p6.nmv_avg_6m_same_elapsed, s.nmv_avg_6m),
     NULLIF(IF(s.is_current_month, p6.nmv_stddev_6m_same_elapsed, s.nmv_stddev_6m),0))
                                                            AS nmv_zscore_6m
  ,IF(s.is_current_month, s.nmv > p6.nmv_max_6m_same_elapsed, s.nmv > s.nmv_max_6m)
                                                            AS is_6m_high
  ,IF(s.is_current_month, s.nmv < p6.nmv_min_6m_same_elapsed, s.nmv < s.nmv_min_6m)
                                                            AS is_6m_low
  ,p6.nmv_avg_6m_same_elapsed
  ,p6.nmv_stddev_6m_same_elapsed
  ,p6.nmv_min_6m_same_elapsed
  ,p6.nmv_max_6m_same_elapsed

   -- ---------- NEW: pace, run-rate and the ask -------------------------------
  ,s.days_elapsed
  ,s.days_total
  ,s.elapsed_share
  ,s.mtd_target_prorated
  ,s.attainment_vs_prorated
  ,IF(s.is_low_target OR s.is_target_invalid, NULL,
      s.nmv_raw - s.month_target)                           AS target_gap_vnd
  ,s.recent_daily_nmv
  ,s.nmv_run_rate_full_month
  ,IF(s.is_low_target OR s.is_target_invalid, NULL,
      SAFE_DIVIDE(s.nmv_run_rate_full_month, NULLIF(s.month_target,0)))
                                                            AS projected_attainment
  ,IF(s.is_low_target OR s.is_target_invalid, NULL,
      s.nmv_run_rate_full_month - s.month_target)           AS projected_gap_vnd
  ,s.required_daily_nmv
   -- > 1 means every remaining day has to beat the days already traded
  ,IF(s.is_low_target OR s.is_target_invalid, NULL,
      SAFE_DIVIDE(s.required_daily_nmv, NULLIF(s.recent_daily_nmv,0)))
                                                            AS required_vs_recent_ratio
  ,IF(IFNULL(s.attainment_vs_full_month, 1) < 1,
      ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY s.country, s.level_2, s.run_id
                         ORDER BY s.month_idx), 0)          AS consecutive_months_missed

   -- ---------- NEW: mix -------------------------------------------------------
  ,SAFE_DIVIDE(s.nmv, NULLIF(s.nmv_country,0))              AS share_of_country_nmv
  ,SAFE_DIVIDE(s.nmv, NULLIF(s.nmv_group,0))                AS share_of_group_nmv

   -- ---------- NEW: trust and completeness -----------------------------------
  ,s.data_complete_through
  ,s.last_date_with_data
  ,s.days_covered
  ,s.days_covered >= s.days_elapsed                         AS is_month_data_complete
  ,s.nmv_excluded_by_cutoff
  ,s.pct_nmv_modelled
  ,DATE_DIFF(p.report_date, s.last_date_with_data, DAY)     AS days_since_last_data
  ,IFNULL(DATE_DIFF(p.report_date, s.last_date_with_data, DAY) > 14, FALSE) AS is_dormant
FROM streak s
CROSS JOIN p
CROSS JOIN mom_window mw
LEFT JOIN prev_capped  pc ON pc.country = s.country AND pc.level_2 = s.level_2
LEFT JOIN prev6_capped p6 ON p6.country = s.country AND p6.level_2 = s.level_2